habitats of the Western Ghats (Whitaker & Captain 2004) (Fig. 4 a). This species may also occur in the far northern dry zone of Sri Lanka. Our sampling indicates that this species is distributed in lowland areas near the coast on the western side of the Western Ghats, the southern tip of Peninsular India and drier parts of Karnataka. While considering the range of A. anomala (Mohapatra et al. 2017), the range of A. oxyrhyncha comb. nov. extends further into the central and east coast of Peninsular India including Odisha and West Bengal. Mostly found in arid and semi-arid habitats in dry deciduous forests, open habitats including scrub forests, coastal forests, and in Indian savannah. We did not find this species during our extensive sampling within the Western Ghats.","","text","",""]]},"87VFL":{"d":[["Brasil coast","17462","mrgid","",""]]},"8CPL":{"d":[["Madagascan","","text","",""]]},"8GMHC":{"d":[["Tibet","","text","",""]]},"8JWJT":{"d":[["Queensland","","text","",""]]},"8JWK3":{"d":[["Guangxi","","text","",""]]},"8K2RP":{"d":[["California","","text","",""]]},"8K6K3":{"d":[["ESP-00 (Canary Is. aggregation)","","text","",""]]},"8NZ7":{"d":[["Australia, Western Australia","","text","native",""]]},"8QFWQ":{"d":[["Germany","48115","mrgid","",""]]},"8SSWB":{"d":[["Oriental(Thailand)","","text","",""]]},"8TB7R":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""]]},"8ZBC":{"d":[["?Kazakhstan; Uzbekistan; Tajikistan","","text","",""]]},"8ZJTG":{"d":[["Middle America","","text","",""]]},"8ZK3G":{"d":[["South America","","text","",""]]},"8ZNLK":{"d":[["W. African Rain Forest","","text","native",""]]},"98Y9T":{"d":[["China (Yunnan)","","text","",""]]},"9CDC4":{"d":[["Afghanistan (Bamyan, Ghazni, Logar, Wardak, Paktia / Khost)","","text","",""]]},"9DWXK":{"d":[["","BZC","tdwg","",""]]},"9DX7K":{"d":[["","COS","tdwg","",""],["","MXC","tdwg","",""],["","MXE","tdwg","",""],["","MXG","tdwg","",""],["","MXN","tdwg","",""],["","MXS","tdwg","",""],["","MXT","tdwg","",""]]},"9GS8L":{"d":[["Indo-West P